# Disposable local/Compose test database only (see compose.yaml, whose
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD is this exact value) -- not a real secret, never a
# production credential.
#
# DELIBERATELY SEPARATE from test.env: test.env is loaded by the plain
# `npm test` (non-DB) pipeline, whose tests (e.g. test/http/
# buildServerRateLimiting.test.mjs, test/http/trustProxy.test.mjs) assert
# on /health/db's response ASSUMING no database is reachable at all --
# db/pool.ts's getPool() lazily connects using whatever PCA_DATABASE_URL
# happens to be in process.env, with no awareness of which test needs it.
# A real PCA_DATABASE_URL in test.env would make those non-DB tests
# silently start talking to the real disposable container (wrong
# assertions, and multiple concurrent test processes contending for the
# same connection pool/locks -- this was caught the hard way: it looked
# exactly like several unrelated test files hanging under `npm test`).
# Only the test:db family of npm scripts loads this file (in addition to
# test.env, via a second --env-file flag), so only they ever see this.
PCA_DATABASE_URL=mysql://root:pca_test_only_not_a_secret@127.0.0.1:33061/pca_test
